gned}-9 & <-3x+8<-5 \\\\ -9-8 & <-3x+8-8<-5-8 \\\\ -17 & <-3x<-13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-3.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-17 & <-3x<-13 \\\\ \\frac{-17}{-3} & >\\frac{-3x}{-3}>\\frac{-13}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{17}{3} & >x>\\frac{13}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe solution can be written as $\\frac{17}{3}>x>\\frac{13}{3}$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n\\frac{13}{3}<x<\\frac{17}{3}\n$$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186069351 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186069351 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-3 \\le 2x - 1 \\le 5$?" 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186069351 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-3\\le 2x-1\\le 5?$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186069351 1074 "We isolate $x$  by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\le 2x-1\\le 5 \\\\ -3+1 & \\le 2x-1+1\\le 5+1 \\\\ -2 & \\le 2x\\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{2} & \\le \\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows. \n\n![](images/76/76b6a19b3104f122989479a681709af3ca0bf8c05c59f76dc2c7707643980398.png)" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186069352 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186069352 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-5 \\le - 2x + 3 \\le 5$?" 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186069352 1071 "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-5\\le -2x+3\\le 5?$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186069352 1074 "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual. \n\nFirst, we apply the addition principle:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & \\le -2x+3\\le 5 \\\\ -5-3 & \\le -2x+3-3\\le 5-3 \\\\ -8 & \\le -2x\\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-2.$ Note that since we are dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality signs. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & \\le -2x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{-8}{-2} & \\ge \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\ge \\frac{2}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{8}{2} & \\ge x\\ge -\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ 4 & \\ge x\\ge -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution can be written as $4\\ge x\\ge -1$, but this is somewhat difficult to read because the larger number is on the left rather than the right. So, we will rewrite the solution by reversing the order of the numbers: \n\n$$\n-1\\le x\\le 4\n$$\n\nWe can represent this solution using a number line, as follows.\n\n![](images/c4/c4f4ab05b534287dc75765b83dc23cbdfe42044aeddea220510668fbc6b8b51c.png)" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186073715 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542138 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186073820 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542154 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186073884 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542159 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186091199 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186091200 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186091201 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186091202 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186091203 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541544 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541678 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541765 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541775 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186091198 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541816 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186091198 1