ute angle formed with the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis. \n\nFor example, let's consider the angles ![](images/1d/1d2f5a08ccb5688494cc87753b29b5569af4bbd93c704c376f30046928f8618e.svg) and ![](images/5b/5b7ef934f94884d2eaceec6dffd5ff9fd12db70a221b3c3b3bce23b6e48efcc1.svg) These angles lie in the first, second, third, and fourth quadrants, respectively. And each of these angles has a reference angle ![](images/27/27ca7b17696552bcbf9d92c69a6ea8dac7e0e56f0f450e12dd1ad3e0a98abc6c.svg) as shown below.\n\n![](images/bf/bfba74ff2c6a69b3db1c9478f5caac4c31578ed93b47302a74d843b04fc6ee85.png)\n\n**Note:** Any reference angle always lies between ![](images/d2/d22511f2212b05e9408f52f8da19a125897737f033bb64f480780f2f024b2091.svg) and ![](images/26/2614c435bff188ded3027f2a8f1ea011b37b41a1d62d2ff4bae181ce9107b5c2.svg) inclusively:\n\n![](images/ac/acc49c928eb9101bcc2ce3c43238a8ed33742d0eb791fca361584d556bca8b9a.svg)" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186111863 1064 "Suppose that we have an angle $\\theta$ in the coordinate plane positioned in the usual way. Its **reference angle**, denoted $\\theta_R$, is the smallest positive acute angle formed with the $x$-axis.\n\nFor example, let's consider the angles\n\n$$\n\\theta=45^\\circ, 135^\\circ, 225^\\circ\n$$\n\nand $315^\\circ$. These angles lie in the first, second, third, and fourth quadrants, respectively. And each of these angles has a reference angle\n\n$$\n\\theta_R = 45^\\circ\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/bf/bfba74ff2c6a69b3db1c9478f5caac4c31578ed93b47302a74d843b04fc6ee85.png)\n\n**Note:** Any reference angle always lies between $0^\\circ$ and $90^\\circ$ inclusively:\n\n$$\n0\\leq \\theta_R \\leq 90^\\circ\n$$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186132091 1078 #edb/ref 17592186132093 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186133963 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542147 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186134342 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186134342 1071 "Evaluate $\\sqrt{7x - 4}$ for $x = 7$." 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186134342 1071 "Evaluate $\\sqrt{7x-4}$ for $x=7.$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186134342 1074 "We replace $x$ with $7$ in the given expression, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{7x-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{7\\cdot 7-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{49-4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{45}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify even further using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{45} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot 5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{5} & = \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186135517 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541820 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186135517 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541820 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186135518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541757 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186135518 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541757 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186138511 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542142 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186138753 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186138753 1071 "The volume $v$ of acid in a test tube measures $10.25\\,\\text{mL}$ to the nearest hundredth of a milliliter. Determine the upper and lower bounds of this measurement.\n\n{{field-1}}$\\text{mL}$\n$\\,\\le v<$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{mL}$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186138753 1071 "The volume $v$ of acid in a test tube measures $10.25mL$ to the nearest hundredth of a milliliter. Determine the upper and lower bounds of this measurement. {{field-1}} $mL$\n$\\le v <$\n{{field-2}} $mL$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186138753 1074 "Our measurement is given to the nearest $0.01\\,\\text{mL}.$ So, the greatest possible error of this measurement is\n\n$$\n\\frac{0.01\\,\\text{mL}}{2}=0.005\\,\\text{mL}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the lower and upper bounds of this measurement as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{lower bound} & =10.25\\,\\text{mL}-0.005\\,\\text{mL} \\\\  & =10.245\\,\\text{mL} \\\\ \\text{upper bound} & =10.25\\,\\text{mL}+0.005\\,\\text{mL} \\\\  & =10.255\\,\\text{mL}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the exact value of $v$ lies between the lower and upper bound, we conclude that\n\n$$\n10.245\\,\\text{mL}\\le v<10.255\\,\\text{mL}.\n$$" 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542137 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542184 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152236 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542207 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542132 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152237 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542171 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542113 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152238 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542168 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152296 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542120 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186152322 1050 420.0 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186156352 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186156353 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186156354 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186156355 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186156356 13194139535918 17592186045417 false] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541579 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541805 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541831 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541859 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186156351 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541886 13194139535918 17592186045417 true] [17592186156351 1078 #edb/ref